## Aim
To visualize monthly temperature and rainfall data using line and scatter plots in Matplotlib.

## Algorithm
1. Start the program and import Matplotlib.
2. Store month names, temperature and rainfall values in lists.
3. Create a line plot for monthly temperature.
4. Add title and axis labels to the line plot.
5. Create a scatter plot for monthly rainfall.
6. Display both plots using `plt.show()`.

## Input

Months = Jan, Feb, Mar, Apr, May, Jun

Temperature = [25, 27, 30, 32, 29, 26]

Rainfall = [10, 20, 35, 50, 80, 100]

## Output

Two graphs are displayed:
1. Line plot showing monthly temperature.
2. Scatter plot showing monthly rainfall.

## Code

```python
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

months = ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr", "May", "Jun"]
temperature = [25, 27, 30, 32, 29, 26]
rainfall = [10, 20, 35, 50, 80, 100]

plt.plot(months, temperature, marker="o")
plt.title("Monthly Temperature")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Temperature")
plt.show()

plt.scatter(months, rainfall)
plt.title("Monthly Rainfall")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Rainfall")
plt.show()
```

## Result
Monthly temperature and rainfall data were successfully visualized using line and scatter plots.

